  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "_zend_hash_del_el",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend_hash.c",
    "description": "_zend_hash_del_el keeps using the Bucket pointer p after calling _zend_hash_del_el_ex. That helper copies/undefines p->val and invokes the HashTable value destructor. For EG(symbol_table), destroying the object executes userland __destruct(), which can mutate the same table. The PoV adds many $GLOBALS entries, causing zend_hash_do_resize() to allocate new bucket storage and free the allocation containing p. Control then returns to _zend_hash_del_el, which dereferences the stale p at `if (p->key)`/`p->key = NULL`, producing the heap-use-after-free. The key must be saved or otherwise handled before invoking the re-entrant value destructor; the callback cannot safely be followed by accesses through p.",
    "conditions": "During request shutdown, shutdown_destructors() reverse-applies zval_call_destructor to EG(symbol_table). A string-keyed global must contain an object with refcount 1 so the callback requests removal. Removing it invokes that object's userland __destruct() through the symbol table's pDestructor. The destructor must insert enough globals into the same non-packed symbol table to trigger zend_hash_do_resize() and free/reallocate arData. After this re-entrant resize, _zend_hash_del_el resumes and reads the old bucket's key. The PoV's ctor object and loop adding 100 `$GLOBALS[\"$i\"]` entries satisfy these constraints."
  },
